# Wolseley 6/80 four-door saloon, 1948-1954.
#
# The six-cylinder Wolseley on the long Morris Six MS shell: 4,496 mm long,
# 1,778 mm wide, 1,600 mm high, 2,794 mm wheelbase; 2,215 cc six. The standard
# British police car of the early 1950s and a director's saloon, with the
# illuminated Wolseley badge in the grille.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolseley_6/80
#
# Colours: Black, Maroon, Dove Grey and Sage Green are documented Wolseley
# finishes of the period.
#
# Weight: 55 in total (black 20, maroon 12, grey 12, green 11), low per section F
# of the gaps doc.
#
# Speed 130 km/h; comfort 100/330 (line). Class 3.
# Dates: 1948-1962, the tail covering later life on British roads.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/wolseley-6-80.blend. References:
# citycars/references/wolseley-6-80/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
name=Wolseley680(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=20
intro_year=1948
intro_month=10
retire_year=1962
retire_month=6
speed=130
class=3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=100
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=330

